`__tests__/provider-integration-e2e.test.ts` is executed; this file contains the
`describe('MCP Client Integration', ...)` block starting at line 375 in the PR diff.

2. Vitest enters the test `it('should handle connection errors gracefully', ...)` at lines
376–392; the first statement in the test body executes `await import('@/lib/mcp/client')`
(line 377).

3. At runtime, Node/Vitest attempts to resolve the module path `@/lib/mcp/client`; a
repo-wide glob search (`Glob` with pattern `**/lib/mcp/client.*` under `/workspace/binG`)
returned "No files found", confirming that no `lib/mcp/client` implementation exists in
the project.

4. Because the dynamic import rejects with a module-not-found error before any `try/catch`
in the test body, the test fails with an unhandled module resolution error rather than the
expected connection error assertion, causing the MCP client integration tests (and likely
the whole provider E2E suite) to fail whenever they are run.
