`executeLocalShellCommand()` at `TerminalPanel.tsx:489-603` creates a directory
`project/foo` and file `project/foo/a.txt` entries in `localFileSystemRef.current` via the
`mkdir` and `touch` cases at 703-752.

3. Run `rm -rf foo` in the same terminal; the `rm` case at `TerminalPanel.tsx:755-779`
computes `targetPath` for `foo` and deletes only the `project/foo` directory entry (line
777) without removing any keys that start with `project/foo/`, leaving `project/foo/a.txt`
still present in the in-memory map.

4. Verify the inconsistency by noting that `ls` at `TerminalPanel.tsx:628-679` no longer
shows `foo` under `project`, but commands like `cat foo/a.txt` still succeed because
`resolveLocalPath()` at 398-432 returns `project/foo/a.txt` and `fs[filePath]` still
exists, demonstrating orphaned child entries after `rm -rf`.
