**Suggestion:** The connection-timeout fallback sets the terminal into `sandbox-cmd` mode with `isConnected: true` but without a valid `sessionId`, so any commands entered in this mode will attempt to send input with an undefined session ID and fail against the backend terminal APIs. [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ⚠️ Terminal status reports connected sandbox without real session.
- ⚠️ Users misled into thinking remote sandbox is available.
- ⚠️ Confusing mode indicator: sandbox-cmd but using local shell.
```
</details>

