<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. In `components/conversation-interface.tsx:30-43`, ensure the Terminal is visible
(`showTerminal` true) so that `TerminalPanel` mounts and `createTerminal()` in
`components/terminal/TerminalPanel.tsx:268-315` auto-invokes `connectTerminal(id)` after 1
s.

2. In `connectTerminal()` at `TerminalPanel.tsx:1924-1993`, if the sandbox backend is slow
or unavailable such that no `connected` message arrives and `sandboxInfo.status` stays
`'creating'`, the 15 s timeout at lines 1965-1991 fires.

3. The timeout handler sets `sandboxInfo: { status: 'active' }`, `isConnected: true`, and
`mode: 'sandbox-cmd'` on the terminal (lines 1976-1984) without ever populating
`sandboxInfo.sessionId`, while printing "Connection timeout. Using command-mode." and a
sandbox-style prompt.

4. Subsequent input is handled by `initXterm`'s `onData` at `TerminalPanel.tsx:1530-1790`:
because `term.mode === 'sandbox-cmd'` but `term.sandboxInfo.sessionId` is falsy, the
sandbox-cmd branch at 1548-1552 is skipped and local shell handling is used instead, so
commands run locally while the status (e.g. `status` command at 1007-1027) incorrectly
reports `Mode: sandbox-cmd` and `Connected: yes` even though no sandbox session is active;
the suggestion slightly misstates this as an "undefined sessionId send," but there is
still a real state/UX inconsistency.
