comments.content:
**Suggestion:** The cleanup effect that saves terminal state is keyed on `sandboxStatus`, so every time the sandbox status changes it runs its cleanup and closes/disposes all terminals and SSE connections, effectively tearing down the terminal whenever the sandbox connects/disconnects instead of only on component unmount. Split the concerns so state persistence happens on status changes, but terminal disposal and session saving only run on unmount. [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Critical 🚨</summary>

```mdx
- ❌ Sandbox connect/disconnect disposes terminals, breaking active sessions.
- ❌ Idle timeout auto-disconnect also tears down all terminals.
```
</details>

```suggestion
  // Persist terminal state when sandbox connection status changes
  useEffect(() => {
    const state = {
      commandHistory: commandHistoryRef.current,
      sandboxConnected: sandboxStatus === 'connected',
      timestamp: Date.now(),
    };
    try {
      localStorage.setItem('terminal-state', JSON.stringify(state));
      console.log('[Terminal] Saved state to localStorage');
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('[Terminal] Failed to save terminal state:', error);
    }
  }, [sandboxStatus]);

  // Save terminal state on unmount/close
  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      // Close terminals and persist sessions
      terminalsRef.current.forEach(t => {
        t.eventSource?.close();
        t.terminal?.dispose();

        saveTerminalSession({
          id: t.id,
          name: t.name,
          commandHistory: commandHistoryRef.current[t.id] || [],
          sandboxInfo: {
            ...t.sandboxInfo,
            status: 'none'
          },
        });
      });
    };
  }, []);
```
<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Open the main conversation UI that renders `TerminalPanel` from
`components/conversation-interface.tsx` (see import at
`/workspace/binG/components/conversation-interface.tsx:12` and usage around line 939 via
Grep).

2. Note the effect in `components/terminal/TerminalPanel.tsx` lines 373–401 (from the PR
hunk) where `useEffect(() => { return () => { ...dispose... } }, [sandboxStatus])`
registers a cleanup that closes `t.eventSource` and calls `t.terminal?.dispose()` for
every terminal whenever `sandboxStatus` changes.

3. Click the sandbox connection button in the Terminal header (button wired to
`toggleSandboxConnection` at `components/terminal/TerminalPanel.tsx` lines 3638–3689),
which transitions `sandboxStatus` from `'disconnected'` to `'connecting'`/`'connected'`.

4. When `sandboxStatus` changes, React runs the cleanup from the previous effect run
(lines 373–401), closing all EventSources and disposing all `xterm` instances without
re‑initializing them; subsequent typing in the terminal no longer echoes and further PTY
connections operate on disposed terminals, effectively breaking the panel while it is
still mounted.
```
</details>
<details>
<summary><b>Prompt for AI Agent 🤖 </b></summary>

```mdx
This is a comment left during a code review.

**Path:** components/terminal/TerminalPanel.tsx
**Line:** 373:401
**Comment:**
	*Logic Error: The cleanup effect that saves terminal state is keyed on `sandboxStatus`, so every time the sandbox status changes it runs its cleanup and closes/disposes all terminals and SSE connections, effectively tearing down the terminal whenever the sandbox connects/disconnects instead of only on component unmount. Split the concerns so state persistence happens on status changes, but terminal disposal and session saving only run on unmount.

Validate the correctness of the flagged issue. If correct, How can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, implement it and please make it concise.
```
</details>
