**Suggestion:** The `file_exists` tool claims to check for both files and directories but only probes files via `readFile`, so it will incorrectly report existing directories as non-existent; using `listDirectory` as a fallback lets you correctly detect directories. [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ⚠️ `file_exists` misreports directories as missing in VFS.
- ⚠️ Future agents relying on directory checks get wrong signals.
- ⚠️ May cause redundant file creation or incorrect planning.
```
</details>

```suggestion
    execute: async ({ path }: { path: string }): Promise<ToolCallResult> => {
      try {
        const userId = getCurrentUserId();
        // First, check if a file exists at this path
        await virtualFilesystem.readFile(userId, path);
        return {
          success: true,
          exists: true,
          type: 'file',
        };
      } catch (error: any) {
        if (error.message?.includes('not found')) {
          try {
            // If no file, check whether there is a directory with this path
            const listing = await virtualFilesystem.listDirectory(userId, path);
            const hasEntries = listing.nodes.length > 0;
            if (hasEntries) {
              return {
                success: true,
                exists: true,
                type: 'directory',
              };
            }
            // No file and no directory contents => treat as not existing
            return {
              success: true,
              exists: false,
            };
          } catch (listError: any) {
            return {
              success: false,
              error: listError.message || 'Failed to check file existence',
            };
          }
        }
        return {
          success: false,
          error: error.message || 'Failed to check file existence',
        };
      }
    },
```
<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Inspect the `file_exists` tool in `lib/mastra/tools/filesystem-tools.ts:240-273`; its
description says "Check if a file or directory exists at the given path", but its
implementation at lines 252-260 only calls `virtualFilesystem.readFile(userId, path)` and
returns `{ exists: true, type: 'file' }` on success, otherwise `{ exists: false }` if the
error message includes "not found".

2. Examine the virtual filesystem directory listing implementation in
`lib/virtual-filesystem/virtual-filesystem-service.ts:246-292`; `listDirectory(ownerId,
directoryPath)` computes a normalized directory path and scans `workspace.files` to build
`nodes` for both files and inferred subdirectories under that path, returning `{ path,
nodes }` even when there is no file exactly at `directoryPath`.

3. In a test or script, create a file inside a subdirectory-only path:

   - `await virtualFilesystem.writeFile('current-user', 'project/src/app.ts',
   'console.log(1);');` (using `writeFile` at `virtual-filesystem-service.ts:86-162`).

   - This implicitly creates a logical directory `project/src`, which
   `listDirectory('current-user', 'project/src')` can enumerate with at least one node for
   `app.ts`.

4. Now call the `file_exists` tool directly:

   - `import { filesystemTools } from '@/lib/mastra/tools/filesystem-tools';`

   - `const tool = filesystemTools.find(t => t.name === 'file_exists')!;`

   - `const result = await tool.execute({ path: 'project/src' });`

   The tool invokes `virtualFilesystem.readFile('current-user', 'project/src')` (lines
   252-255), which throws `Error("File not found: project/src")` per `readFile` at
   `virtual-filesystem-service.ts:74-81`, leading the catch block at lines 261-266 to
   return `{ success: true, exists: false }` even though
   `virtualFilesystem.listDirectory('current-user', 'project/src')` (lines 246-292) would
   return a non-empty `nodes` array and demonstrate that the directory is effectively
   present.
```
</details>
