**Suggestion:** In the GET handler, `authManager.getUserId` throws on invalid or expired tokens, but the thrown error is caught by the outer try/catch and converted into a 500 response, so invalid JWTs produce "Failed to retrieve API keys" (500) instead of a 401 "Invalid token" as intended. [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ❌ GET /api/user/api-keys returns 500 on invalid tokens.
- ⚠️ Auth failures inflate server-error metrics and monitoring alerts.
```
</details>

```suggestion
