```
<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Start the Next.js app so the route `app/api/user/api-keys/route.ts` is active; the GET
handler is defined at lines 18–58.

2. Send an HTTP GET request to `GET /api/user/api-keys` with an `Authorization` header
like `Bearer invalid-token` so it passes the `startsWith('Bearer ')` check at lines 21–27
but is not a valid JWT.

3. The GET handler extracts the token at line 29 and calls `authManager.getUserId(token)`
at line 30, which delegates to `getUserId` in `lib/backend/auth.ts` lines 38–85;
`jwtVerify` (lines 57–62) throws for invalid/expired tokens and `getUserId` rethrows as
`Error('Invalid JWT token')` or `Error('JWT token has expired')` (lines 76–82).

4. This error is caught only by the outer `try/catch` in the GET handler at lines 19–57,
which logs `'Failed to get API keys:'` and returns a 500 JSON `{ error: 'Failed to
retrieve API keys' }` (lines 51–55); the `if (!userId)` 401 branch at lines 32–37 is never
reached for invalid/expired tokens.
```
</details>
