**Suggestion:** In the POST handler, an invalid or expired JWT causes `authManager.getUserId` to throw, which is caught only by the outer try/catch and returned as a 500 "Failed to save API keys" error, so authentication failures are misclassified as server errors instead of returning a 401 "Invalid token". [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ❌ POST /api/user/api-keys returns 500 on invalid tokens.
- ⚠️ UI may show generic failure instead of reauth prompt.
```
</details>

