```
<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Start the Next.js app so `app/api/user/api-keys/route.ts` is active; the POST handler
is defined at lines 64–114.

2. Send an HTTP POST to `POST /api/user/api-keys` with header `Authorization: Bearer
invalid-token` and any JSON body so it passes the Bearer check at lines 67–72 but uses an
invalid/expired JWT.

3. The POST handler extracts the token at line 75 and calls `authManager.getUserId(token)`
at line 76; `authManager.getUserId` delegates to `getUserId` in `lib/backend/auth.ts`
(lines 38–85), where `jwtVerify` throws for invalid/expired tokens and `getUserId`
rethrows as an `Error` (lines 76–82).

4. This exception is caught only by the outer `try/catch` in the POST handler at lines
65–113, which logs `'Failed to save API keys:'` and returns a 500 JSON `{ error: 'Failed
to save API keys' }` (lines 107–111); the intended `if (!userId)` 401 branch at lines
78–83 is never invoked for authentication failures.
```
</details>
