**Suggestion:** In the DELETE handler, `authManager.getUserId` throws for invalid/expired tokens and the error is caught only by the outer try/catch, causing a 500 "Failed to delete API keys" response instead of returning a 401 "Invalid token" for authentication failures. [logic error]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ❌ DELETE /api/user/api-keys returns 500 on invalid tokens.
- ⚠️ Users see server error when deleting with expired sessions.
```
</details>

```suggestion
