```
<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Start the Next.js app so `app/api/user/api-keys/route.ts` is active; the DELETE handler
is defined at lines 120–155.

2. Send an HTTP DELETE to `DELETE /api/user/api-keys` with header `Authorization: Bearer
invalid-token` so it passes the Bearer prefix check at lines 123–128 but provides an
invalid or expired JWT.

3. The DELETE handler extracts the token at line 131 and calls
`authManager.getUserId(token)` at line 132; `authManager.getUserId` uses `getUserId` from
`lib/backend/auth.ts` (lines 38–85), which throws for invalid/expired tokens after
`jwtVerify` fails (lines 57–62 and 76–82).

4. The thrown error is caught only by the outer `try/catch` in the DELETE handler at lines
121–155, which logs `'Failed to delete API keys:'` and returns a 500 JSON `{ error:
'Failed to delete API keys' }` (lines 149–153); the `if (!userId)` 401 branch at lines
134–139 is not executed for authentication failures.
```
