Missing authentication on image generation endpoint. The route is publicly accessible and uses provider API keys (Mistral/Replicate) to perform costly image generation. This allows anonymous abuse to consume credits and compute.

Example (no auth checks before provider usage):
```ts
export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  ...
  const registry = getDefaultRegistry();
  const initializedRegistry = registry.initializeAll({
    mistral: { apiKey: process.env.MISTRAL_API_KEY },
    replicate: { apiKey: process.env.REPLICATE_API_TOKEN },
  });
  ...
  const result = await initializedRegistry.generateWithFallback(params, undefined, controller.signal)
}
```
Remediation:
- Require authentication (JWT/session) before processing requests
- Apply per-user rate limits/quotas and request validation (max images, size, steps)
- Consider allowlisting models/providers


For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/747b0345-a959-4d87-8d5f-4678b9d4eef1).

**Provide feedback**: Reply with whether this is a valid vulnerability or false positive to help improve Corridor's accuracy.

