These Docker control endpoints only check that the user is authenticated, but do not verify authorization/ownership of the target containers. As written, any authenticated user can list all containers and execute commands (even with a limited whitelist), read logs (possible secret leakage), and start/stop/remove arbitrary containers accessible via the Docker socket:

- List containers:
```ts
// app/api/docker/containers/route.ts
const containers = await docker.listContainers({ all: true });
```
- Execute in container:
```ts
// app/api/docker/exec/route.ts
const container = docker.getContainer(containerId);
const exec = await container.exec({ Cmd: validation.sanitizedCmd!, AttachStdout: true, AttachStderr: true });
```
- Logs/start/stop/remove:
```ts
// app/api/docker/logs/[id]/route.ts -> container.logs(...)
// app/api/docker/start/[id]/route.ts -> container.start()
// app/api/docker/stop/[id]/route.ts -> container.stop()
// app/api/docker/remove/[id]/route.ts -> container.remove({ force: true })
```

Impact:
- Privilege escalation: any authenticated user can affect unrelated services/tenants, disrupt workloads, and exfiltrate sensitive logs.

Remediation:
- Enforce strict authorization before any Docker operation (e.g., only admins; or map containers to owning users and verify ownership).
- Consider isolating Docker control behind an internal admin-only API/service.
- For logs/exec, add explicit allowlists and redact/limit outputs; for start/stop/remove, enforce role checks.


For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/5ae6481d-590c-4afb-adb5-5a9967330c5c).

**Provide feedback**: Reply with whether this is a valid vulnerability or false positive to help improve Corridor's accuracy.

This endpoint exposes stateful agent functionality without any authentication. It can create sandboxes and run workflows/tools on provider backends:

```ts
export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  // ...
  if (!targetSandboxId) {
    const sandboxProvider = await getSandboxProvider(DEFAULT_SANDBOX_PROVIDER);
    const sandbox = await sandboxProvider.createSandbox({ language: 'typescript', resources: { cpu: 1, memory: 512 } });
    targetSandboxId = sandbox.id;
  }
}
```

Impact:
- Unauthenticated attackers can create/abuse compute resources and trigger backend operations, violating the guardrail that tool/sandbox operations must require authentication.

Remediation:
- Require authentication (`verifyAuth`/`resolveRequestAuth`) at the start of the handler and reject unauthenticated requests.
- Optionally enforce quotas/rate limits per user and audit all executions.


For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/0c5fc5bd-479f-45df-a159-b300a48364fc).

**Provide feedback**: Reply with whether this is a valid vulnerability or false positive to help improve Corridor's accuracy.

Untrusted markdown link URLs are used directly as the `href` value without sanitization. This enables `javascript:` URLs to execute code when clicked (XSS).

Vulnerable code:
```tsx
<a
  href={href}
  className={`text-purple-300 hover:text-purple-200 underline inline-flex items-center gap-1 ${
    layout.isMobile && dynamicStyles.overflowStrategy === 'ellipsis'
      ? 'truncate inline-block max-w-full'
      : 'break-all'
  }`}
  {...props}
>
  {children}
  {isEmbeddable && (
    <span ... onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('open-embed-plugin', { detail: { url: href, suggestedPlugin, embedInfo } })); }}>
      ...
    </span>
  )}
</a>
```

Impact: A malicious link like `[click me](javascript:alert(1))` in message content will execute arbitrary JavaScript when clicked.

Remediation: Validate and allowlist URL schemes before assigning to `href`. For example, only allow `http:`, `https:`, and optionally `mailto:`. Also consider adding `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"` and `target=\"_blank\"` for external links.

```suggestion
href={typeof href === 'string' && /^(https?:|mailto:)/i.test(href) ? href : '#'}
```

For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/0e8bbcf9-8a7f-4b9f-9df4-e5a1bb529e04).

**Provide feedback**: Reply with whether this is a valid vulnerability or false positive to help improve Corridor's accuracy.

