This webhook only verifies the signature if a secret is configured. When `COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set, the handler proceeds to parse and process the webhook payload without any authentication:

```ts
const secret = process.env.COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET;
if (secret) {
  // verify signature
  ...
}

// Without a secret, processing continues here with no verification
const payload = JSON.parse(body);
const result = await handleComposioWebhookWithPayload(payload);
```

This creates a missing authentication vulnerability for a critical endpoint — an attacker can POST arbitrary payloads to this webhook to trigger internal processing.

Remediation:
- Require `COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` in production and reject requests if it is not configured (e.g., return 503 with a clear error). Optionally allow skipping verification only in explicit development mode with a dedicated flag.
- Always fail closed if signature validation fails or no signature is provided.

For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/59e58d2c-0560-453c-9b15-c3fd33f52b0c).

