comments.content:
The endpoint allows executing npx commands without authentication when VISUAL_EDITOR_SECRET is not set (empty string by default). This exposes remote code execution over the internet, since npx runs third-party CLIs on the server.

Vulnerable logic:
```ts
const SECRET = process.env.VISUAL_EDITOR_SECRET ?? "";
...
// ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if (SECRET) {
  const auth = req.headers.get("x-visual-editor-secret") ?? "";
  if (auth !== SECRET) {
    return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
  }
}
```
When SECRET is empty, the check is skipped and any caller can invoke the command execution path:
```ts
const child = spawn("npx", [baseCmd, subCmd, ...sanitizedArgs], {
  cwd: path.resolve(projectPath),
  env: { ...process.env, FORCE_COLOR: "0" },
  shell: false,
});
```
This enables unauthenticated RCE with the server’s privileges, even if the baseCmd is allowlisted.

Impact: Critical. Internet users can execute arbitrary code via allowed CLIs (e.g., installing/running code from npm) in the server’s filesystem.

Remediation:
- Enforce authentication unconditionally. If VISUAL_EDITOR_SECRET is not configured, deny all requests by default.
- Additionally, require user authentication/authorization (e.g., JWT/session) and restrict to admin roles in production.
- Consider disabling this endpoint altogether unless explicitly enabled in a secure environment.


For more details, see the [finding in Corridor](https://app.corridor.dev/projects/9b474c20-ed45-4b3a-ad03-b76d21c45b95/findings/4bdd1799-955d-45e6-8503-624342c253ef).

**Provide feedback**: Reply with whether this is a valid vulnerability or false positive to help improve Corridor's accuracy.

